@j62268781-alt/dsh-agent-browser README · 决策（`browser_run`：Jev + 上游 LLM 低成本闭环）：判断走 [`dsh-judgment`](../dsh-judgment/README.md)：在 **设置 → 决策** 里建一条连接，
把用途名 `browser.action` 指向它（默认值就是这个）。换厂商/模型/密钥只改那里，不动本插件。

---

@j62268781-alt/dsh-agent-browser README · dsh-agent-browser：> Why not MCP: `agent-browser mcp` injects dozens of atomic actions into the prompt globally, and it
> **structurally cannot** provide an in-plugin bounded loop, per-step freshness gating, an action
> ledger, or a settings page. Full reasoning in [DESIGN.md](DESIGN.md) §1.2 (Chinese).

@j62268781-alt/dsh-agent-browser README · Bundled skill：`pnpm probe` spawns a real browser to verify the version floor, ref parsing, ref-based clicking, and
that a stale ref pointing at a deleted element is rejected instead of clicking something else
(the same-name ordinal fallback documented in DESIGN §1.1 is a known CLI caveat, not covered by the probe).

@j62268781-alt/dsh-agent-browser README · Performance (measured, agent-browser 0.38.2)：`spawn /bin/echo` 1.2ms · `spawn bash -c …` 1.4ms (bash is *more* expensive, not less) ·
`agent-browser --version` through the PATH Node wrapper 57.3ms ·
**native binary** `--version` 3.1ms / `get title` 3.7ms / `snapshot -i` 5.1ms / `click @e2` 16.8ms.

@j62268781-alt/dsh-agent-browser README · Development：```bash
pnpm install && pnpm build && pnpm test && pnpm verify:remote && pnpm probe
```
